complaint_what_happened:
I was targeted by a sophisticated voice phishing and spoofing scam where fraudsters approached me via phone call spoofing the XXXX XXXX in XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, and XXXX XXXX XXXX to manipulate my account details. I have filed for an investigation with the local sheriffs office ( IRC Florida ), filed a fraud and identity theft report with the FTC, and am working to get in touch with the state attorney generals office.

I had 2 paypal accounts and both accounts were compromised in the phishing, spoofing scam. After talking to local police who advised that I close any accounts that I dont use, I closed one of my accounts. A couple of days later, I received an email that a claim had been brought up against me. Below are the transactions that I recognized as fraudulent and unauthorized in one of my accounts. As for the other account that is now closed and unaccessible, I can not provide anything as I do not have access to the Paypal resolution center. I spoke to 5 different associates and no-one was able to provide a resolution. The most recent call being with an associate named XXXX on XX/XX/year>. 

XX/XX/year> XXXX XXXX : XXXX XXXX XX/XX/year> XXXX XXXX : {$2400.00} XX/XX/year> XXXX XXXX : {$2700.00} XX/XX/year>XXXX XXXX  : {$10.00} XX/XX/year>XXXX XXXX : {$970.00}

Someone fraudulently used my card, possibly the merchant to charge my credit card and for the last 8 months I have tried to get Chase to reverse it. According to their own terms of service on the card, I am not liable for these fraudulent charges. 
They need to reverse them back to the merchant and credit my account. 

